## Why this is likely a False Positive
When a website returns a 200 OK status for completely contradictory technologies on the same domain (like WordPress's /wp-admin/ and Apache Tomcat's /manager/html at the same time), it usually means the server uses a catch-all routing rule.
Instead of showing a 404 Not Found error page for folders that do not exist, the server handles unknown URLs by redirecting the user back to the main homepage or a standard landing page with a 200 OK status. Your scanner sees the 200 OK and falsely flags it as a "hit."
